@startuml BackupRestoreServer
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Server Admin" as Admin
actor "Scheduler" as Scheduler
actor "File Storage" as Storage
actor "Monitoring" as Monitoring
actor "Player" as Player

rectangle "Backup & Restore" {
  usecase "Initiate Backup" as UC_Backup
  usecase "Upload Backup" as UC_Upload
  usecase "Record Audit Entry" as UC_Audit
  usecase "Notify Stakeholders" as UC_Notify
  usecase "Initiate Restore" as UC_Restore
  usecase "Verify & Migrate Backup" as UC_Verify
  usecase "Rollback on Failure" as UC_Rollback
  usecase "Manage Retention" as UC_Retention

  ' optional/alternative flows
  usecase "Incremental Backup" as UC_Incremental
  usecase "Dry-run Restore (staging)" as UC_DryRun
}

Admin --> UC_Backup : manual
Scheduler --> UC_Backup : scheduled
UC_Backup --> UC_Upload
UC_Upload --> Storage
UC_Upload --> UC_Audit
UC_Audit --> Monitoring
UC_Audit --> Admin
UC_Upload --> UC_Notify
Admin --> UC_Restore
UC_Restore --> UC_Verify
UC_Verify --> UC_Rollback : on failure
UC_Restore --> UC_Notify
UC_Retention ..> UC_Upload : <<include>>
UC_Retention ..> Storage : <<use>>

' alternative links
UC_Backup ..> UC_Incremental : <<include>>
UC_Restore ..> UC_DryRun : <<extend>>

' Error/alt flows as usecases
rectangle "Error / Recovery Flows" {
  usecase "Network Failure / Retry" as E_Net
  usecase "Storage Quota Exceeded" as E_Quota
  usecase "Checksum Mismatch / Corrupt" as E_Corrupt
  usecase "Version Incompatibility" as E_Version
  usecase "Concurrent Restore Conflict" as E_Conflict
  usecase "Partial Restore Failure" as E_Partial
}

UC_Upload ..> E_Net : handles
UC_Upload ..> E_Quota : may cause
UC_Verify ..> E_Corrupt : may detect
UC_Verify ..> E_Version : may detect
UC_Restore ..> E_Conflict : may detect
UC_Restore ..> E_Partial : may cause
E_Partial ..> UC_Rollback : triggers

note top of UC_Backup
Preconditions:
- Admin authenticated
- Server accessible & read permissions available
- Storage reachable & quota available
- Backup format compatible
end note

note left of UC_Backup
Backup success (README):
- Backup stored, indexed, retrievable, audit logged
end note

note bottom of UC_Restore
Postconditions (success):
- Server state restored and validated
Postconditions (failure):
- No production data loss (rollback) or Admin notified
end note

note right of E_Net
Recovery:
- Retry with backoff
- Provide resumable upload
- Notify Admin if persistent
end note

note right of E_Corrupt
Recovery:
- Reject & request re-upload
- Attempt restore from previous backup
end note

note right of E_Version
Recovery:
- Attempt migration tool
- If impossible, abort and list required steps
end note

@enduml